  rules: [
    "1️⃣ ARGUMENT STRUCTURE NIMA?\n\nAkademik yozuvda to'liq argument 3 qismdan iborat:\n\n📌 CLAIM (da'vo): asosiy fikr yoki pozitsiya\n  It is widely believed that technology improves education.\n\n📌 EVIDENCE (dalil): faktlar, statistika, misollar\n  Studies show that students using digital tools score 20% higher.\n\n📌 EXPLANATION (tushuntirish): dalilni da'voga bog'lash\n  This demonstrates that technology enhances learning outcomes.\n\n🔴 Da'vo + dalilsiz = bo'sh fikr\n🔴 Dalil + tushuntirishsiz = noto'liq argument",
    "2️⃣ CLAIM (DA'VO) IFODALASH\n\nKuchli da'vo — aniq, bahsli, qo'llab-quvvatlanishi mumkin:\n\nDIRECT CLAIM:\n  Technology is essential for modern education.\n  Regular exercise significantly reduces stress.\n\nHEDGED CLAIM (ehtiyotkor):\n  Technology appears to be beneficial for education.\n  Exercise tends to reduce stress in most individuals.\n\nREPORTED CLAIM:\n  It is argued / claimed / suggested that technology improves...\n  Researchers contend that physical activity...\n\n🔴 'I think' yoki 'I believe' akademik yozuvda zaif — ko'proq 'It is argued / evidence suggests' ishlatiladi",
    "3️⃣ EVIDENCE (DALIL) TURLARI\n\nSTATISTICS (raqamlar):\n  According to WHO, 80% of adults do not exercise enough.\n  A 2023 study found that...\n\nEXPERT OPINION (ekspert fikri):\n  Professor Smith argues that...\n  Leading researchers suggest that...\n\nEXAMPLES (misollar):\n  For instance, Finland's education system demonstrates...\n  A case in point is the success of...\n\nLOGICAL REASONING (mantiq):\n  If children read daily, they naturally develop larger vocabularies.\n\n🔴 Bir turda qolib ketmang — aralash foydalaning",
    "4️⃣ COUNTERARGUMENT VA REFUTATION\n\nKuchli argument = qarama-qarshi fikrni ham ko'rib chiqadi:\n\nCONCESSION (tan olish):\n  Admittedly, technology can be distracting.\n  It is true that not everyone has access to digital devices.\n  While some argue that screen time is harmful,\n\nREBUTTAL (rad etish):\n  ...the benefits far outweigh the drawbacks.\n  ...this issue can be addressed through digital literacy programmes.\n  ...the overall educational impact remains positive.\n\nPATTERN:\n  While/Although [opponent's view], [your stronger point].\n  Even though [concession], [rebuttal].\n\n🔴 Refutation = concession + stronger counterpoint (not just denial)",
    "5️⃣ LINKING EXPRESSIONS FOR ARGUMENTS\n\nADDING POINTS:\n  Furthermore, Moreover, In addition, Besides, What is more,\n\nCONTRASTING:\n  However, Nevertheless, On the other hand, In contrast, Whereas,\n\nSHOWING RESULT:\n  Therefore, Thus, Consequently, As a result, Hence,\n\nGIVING EXAMPLES:\n  For instance, For example, Such as, A case in point is,\n\nCONCLUDING:\n  In conclusion, To summarise, Overall, In sum,\n\n🔴 Har bir paragrafda kamida 1 ta linking expression ishlatiladi",
    "6️⃣ PARAGRAPH STRUCTURE — PEEL\n\nP — POINT: da'voni yozing\n  Technology has transformed modern education.\n\nE — EVIDENCE: dalil keltiring\n  According to UNESCO, online learning grew by 900% in the past decade.\n\nE — EXPLANATION: tushuntiring\n  This significant growth indicates that learners worldwide recognize the value of digital tools.\n\nL — LINK: keyingi fikrga bog'lang\n  This further supports the argument that investment in technology is essential.\n\n🔴 PEEL = argumentni mantiqan tuzilgan holda ifodalash",
    "7️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA XATOLAR\n\n• 'I think technology is good' → 'It is argued that technology enhances...' yoki 'Evidence suggests...'\n• Da'vo va dalilni birlashtirmaslik:\n  XATO: Technology is good. Students use it.\n  TO'G'RI: Technology improves outcomes, as evidenced by the 20% score increase observed in digital classrooms.\n• Refutationsiz argument yozish — kuchsiz ko'rinadi\n• 'But' bilan jumlani boshlash — akademik emas; 'However' ishlatiladi\n• 'Also' o'rniga 'Furthermore / Moreover' ishlatiladi",
  ],
