      id: 'hedged-claims',
      title: 'Hedging in Academic Arguments',
      rule: "Akademik yozuvda 100% da'vo qo'pol ko'rinadi. Hedging = ehtiyotkor da'vo:\n\nMODALS:\n  may, might, could, should\n  Technology could improve outcomes.\n\nADVERBS:\n  arguably, possibly, potentially, apparently\n  This is arguably the most effective approach.\n\nVERBS:\n  tend to, appear to, seem to, suggest\n  The data suggests that...\n  Students tend to perform better when...\n\nNOUN PHRASES:\n  in many cases, to some extent, in general\n  To some extent, this approach is effective.\n\n🔴 Hedging ≠ weakness — it shows academic precision",
      mnemonic: "Hedge = protection. Academic writers hedge to show they're being precise, not arrogant. 'The sun rises' = fact. 'Technology improves...' = hedged claim.",
