  rules: [
    "1️⃣ PARAPHRASING NIMA?\n\nParaphrasing = boshqa so'zlar bilan qayta ifodalash, ma'no o'zgarmagan holda.\n\nASLI:\n  Climate change is primarily caused by human industrial activity.\n\nPARAPHRAZ:\n  Human industrial processes are the main driver of climate change.\n\nXULOSA (Summary):\n  Human activity causes climate change. (shorter, main idea only)\n\n🔴 Paraphrase ≠ o'g'irlash: hech bo'lmaganda 3 o'zgartirish kerak\n🔴 Summary = faqat asosiy fikr; paraphrase = xuddi shuncha ma'lumot",
    "2️⃣ PARAPHRASE USULLARI\n\nUSUL 1 — SYNONYM:\n  increase → rise, grow, surge, climb, escalate\n  significant → notable, considerable, substantial\n  show → demonstrate, reveal, indicate, suggest\n\nUSUL 2 — WORD FORM CHANGE:\n  verb → noun: develop → development; achieve → achievement\n  adj → noun: effective → effectiveness; important → importance\n  active → passive: Studies show → It has been shown\n\nUSUL 3 — STRUCTURE CHANGE:\n  Subordinate → Main: Although X, Y → Y, despite X\n  Relative → Participle: The report which was published → The published report\n\nUSUL 4 — REPORTING VERB + CITATION:\n  Smith (2023) argues / maintains / contends / notes that...\n  According to Brown (2022), ...\n  As Jones (2021) observes, ...\n\n🔴 Barcha 4 usulni birga ishlating",
    "3️⃣ REPORTING VERBS (Hisobot Fe'llari)\n\nNEUTRAL (neytral):\n  say, state, note, observe, indicate, suggest, find\n\nSTRONG AGREEMENT:\n  confirm, demonstrate, prove, show, establish\n  The study confirms that...\n\nCAUTIOUS / HEDGED:\n  suggest, imply, appear to show, seem to indicate\n  The data suggests that...\n\nCRITICAL:\n  argue, contend, claim, assert, maintain\n  Critics argue that...\n\nCONTRASTING:\n  acknowledge, concede, admit (followed by but/however)\n  Smith (2023) acknowledges that X; however, ...\n\n🔴 Reporting verb choice = stance expression",
    "4️⃣ SUMMARISING (XULOSA YOZISH)\n\nXulosa = asosiy fikrni qisqacha ifodalash\n\nSTEP 1: Asosiy g'oyani aniqlang\nSTEP 2: Tafsilotlarni olib tashlang\nSTEP 3: Yangi so'zlar bilan qayta yozing\nSTEP 4: Manba ko'rsating\n\nEXAMPLE:\nOriginal (50 words): 'Research conducted by the WHO in 2023 involving 10,000 participants across 15 countries revealed that individuals who exercised for at least 30 minutes per day showed a 40% reduction in reported anxiety and a 35% improvement in overall mood scores compared to sedentary individuals.'\n\nSummary (15 words): 'A WHO study (2023) found that daily exercise significantly improves mental health outcomes.'\n\n🔴 Summary = 20-30% of original length",
    "5️⃣ CITATION PATTERNS\n\nIN-TEXT CITATION:\n  According to Smith (2023), exercise reduces anxiety.\n  Smith (2023) argues that exercise reduces anxiety.\n  Exercise reduces anxiety (Smith, 2023).\n  As Smith (2023) notes, 'Exercise reduces anxiety by 40%.'\n\nREPORTING + PARAPHRASE:\n  Brown (2022) suggests that digital tools tend to improve student engagement.\n  Research by Jones et al. (2021) indicates that...\n\nPLURAL AUTHORS:\n  Smith and Brown (2023) contend that...\n  Smith et al. (2023) demonstrate that... (3+ authors)\n\n🔴 et al. = 'and others' (Latin: et alii)",
    "6️⃣ PLAGIARISM OLDINI OLISH\n\nPLAGIARISM = o'zganing so'zlarini o'zingizniki kabi ishlatish\n\nQUITE DIFFERENT ENOUGH:\n  Change: words, word order, word class, structure\n  Keep: same meaning, same logic\n\nNOT ENOUGH CHANGE:\n  Original: 'Climate change is mainly caused by human activity.'\n  Weak paraphrase: 'Climate change is mainly caused by human actions.' (only one word changed!)\n\nGOOD PARAPHRASE:\n  'Human industrial processes represent the primary driver of global warming.'\n  (word class: caused→processes/driver, human→human industrial, mainly→primary)\n\n🔴 ALWAYS add citation even when paraphrasing",
    "7️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA XATOLAR\n\n• Faqat bir so'zni o'zgartirish = weak paraphrase (plagiarism xavfi)\n• Iqtibos belgisiz to'g'ridan-to'g'ri ko'chirish\n• 'According to Smith, ...' ni vergulsiz yozish:\n  XATO: According to Smith the results show...\n  TO'G'RI: According to Smith, the results show...\n• 'Smith says' — juda informal; 'Smith argues / maintains / contends' yaxshiroq\n• Xulosa (summary) da haddan ko'p detal qoldirish",
  ],
